{
  "version": "1.7.8",
  "changelog": "Save round trip now uses Joshua's close/reopen design: the push leg closes its connection, then a fresh connection is opened for the proof download (fixes 'Remote end closed connection without response'). Failure messages are stage-accurate \u2014 they say whether the push itself failed or the push landed but the proof copy could not be downloaded back. Menu groups gain a per-group 'starts expanded / starts collapsed' setting, stored in menu_layout.json and honored by the game. Also includes the 1.7.7 global save protocol (save locally, push to GitHub, re-download and display the GitHub copy as proof), since the channel was previously at 1.7.6.",
